  "notes": "Reggae-inflected Swedish europop — the \"China reggae\" fusion. This is the one entry in the 1990s block whose identity is explicitly NOT a four-on-the-floor kick: the research says the identity is \"the offbeat keyboard skank on the 2nd and 4th 8th of each beat\", with a \"light programmed kick (not always on all four)\", \"a quiet snare or rimshot on 2&4\", and percussion \"deliberately thin so the skank reads\". That is why the kick drops to 2-4 hits anchored on 1 and 3, the snare carries a rimshot layer with almost no ghosting, the open hat is nearly absent, and the perc gain sits at -7 dB. The bass is the single most distinctive parameter the entry names — \"a syncopated synth bass playing a reggae-derived line that leaves beat 1 empty\" — encoded as an independent riff at 0.6 roots with a 0.5 anticipation so the downbeat is vacated. Harmony is the stated i-VI-III-VII / i-VII-VI with a relative-major chorus lift. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every velocity, density and probability above: the entry gives adjectives (\"light\", \"quiet\", \"thin\") and no numbers, and the tempo band is lane-derived by the entry's own admission. ⚠ The two-sisters close-harmony vocal is encoded only as a narrow interval spread and a low-ornament contour; the counter sits an octave below rather than a third, because the schema's register offset has no third.",
